{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Gateway admin rate limits API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Request, token and concurrency limits for inference, per organization, team, service account and API key, the levels budgets have. Authenticated with a session cookie or an agent token (`Authorization: Bearer gwa_\u2026`), which acts only in its agent's organization. Every limit covering a request applies: the organization's, the team's of the key's team, the service account's, and the key's own. A limit counts reservations, so a request counts toward `requests_per_minute` when admitted (in a sliding 60-second window) and toward `max_concurrent` until it finishes or the expiry worker closes its expired reservation (within its time-to-live plus the worker's interval). Toward `tokens_per_minute` (in the same window) a request counts the most it may use (its input bound plus its output cap) while it runs, then the tokens its provider reported once it is settled, or none if it was released without usage; a request only a smaller output cap fits is admitted with that cap, and one whose input bound and reasoning allowance, with one output token, are more than the limit is refused with no retry that would help (`Retry-After: 60`). A failover attempt counts in the second of the request it continues. Batches count one admission each toward `requests_per_minute`. Creating a batch is refused while single requests in flight are at `max_concurrent` or a token window is used up, but an open batch does not count toward `max_concurrent` (so it does not cap open batches), and batches count no tokens. The window counts whole seconds, so it may count up to one second more than the last 60. Idempotent replays of an inference request are never limited. A request over a limit is rejected before anything is reserved with 429 `rate_limit_exceeded` (requests or tokens per minute) or `concurrency_limit_exceeded` and `Retry-After` in whole seconds; the problem's `scope` and `limit` name the level and the limit reached."
  },
  "security": [
    {
      "session": []
    },
    {
      "agentToken": []
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
